      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define “physiological assessment” or describe it as evaluating bodily responses or reactions; it only mentions “verbal and physiological assessment” without an explicit definition or mechanism.",
        "While the packet supports using assessments in response to stimuli inducing fear, sadness, and disgust, it does not support the broader framing that the physiological component measures “responses that occur when exposed to emotionally meaningful stimuli.”",
        "The definition’s general scope (“used alongside verbal assessment to help understand responses to emotions like fear, sadness, and disgust”) is only partially supported: the packet indicates fear/sadness/disgust stimuli and the coexistence of verbal and physiological assessment, but provides no supporting detail for what the physiological assessment specifically entails."
